      'Seven states added: 73 guides, directory 193 -> 266 guides across 26 states. NEW: Idaho (6), California (16), Michigan (12), Pennsylvania (14). PORTED from the LeadTrap product and completed: Hawaii (9), Iowa (8), Oklahoma (8) - those files existed only in LeadTrap, lacked every structured field, and a month-old re-verification found 35 stale facts between them (e.g. Oklahoma diagnosing-provider list and 2-year evaluation recency per OAC 317:30-5-313 rev. 9/1/2025; Iowa rule renumbering and H.F. 330 removing mandate caps from 1/1/2026; Hawaii QI-2431 read in full and Ohana Health Plan exiting QUEST 12/31/2026). Every new guide carries all 17 structured facts (assessment/treatment PA, diagnosis, 6 delivery rules, 8 intake gates) under the verified-only contract; each commercial guide carries its state autism-mandate rows. Shape notes intake teams need: Idaho Medicaid pays ABA as CHIS on HCPCS codes (Magellan stopped 97151-97158 on 12/1/2025), no diagnosis required, and Idaho has neither an autism statute (DOI Bulletin 18-02 is the floor) nor behavior-analyst licensure; Medi-Cal BHT is for under-21 regardless of diagnosis via the county Medi-Cal plan, with Regional Centers paying last, and California has no behavior-analyst license (QASP tiers); Michigan Medicaid ABA is carved out to the PIHP/CMH system, not the Medicaid Health Plans, and the PIHP re-procurement for 10/1/2026 is unconfirmed; Pennsylvania MA pays ABA as IBHS through the county HealthChoices BH-MCO for any BH diagnosis under 21, Act 62 caps at \$51,908 (2026, CPI-adjusted) for large-group insured plans, and PH-95 keeps MA open as secondary regardless of parental income. Two template issues in existing Optum and Aetna guides surfaced during the build and are logged as VC-039 and VC-040 rather than applied unverified.',
