    summary:
      'Visitor-gap round 2 (2026-10-01), from the payer-chat logs read this run (55 visitor questions since 9/23, internal and test entries excluded; no visitor identity recorded). NEW GUIDE: horizon-bcbs-new-jersey (Horizon BCBSNJ commercial) — a visitor asked whether Horizon NJ commercial restricts ABA in school: until 11/30/2026 Horizon authorizes ABA hours only outside school; from 12/1/2026 (Medical Policy 165 revision) ABA may be approved during non-instructional school periods if it does not duplicate the IEP. NEW TOPICS fanned out: retro-authorization (all 9 NJ guides, TRICARE/CHAMPVA/national payers, and the NC, MD, GA, IN, CO, KS, AZ Medicaid programs and plans); out-of-state providers / interstate telehealth (state licensure law plus each payer\'s own credentialing rule on 52 guides in NC, MD, GA, IN, CO, KS, AZ and the national and military guides — e.g. NC G.S. 108C-9(e) bars BCBAs from enrolling as out-of-state Medicaid providers from 8/2/2026; Optum, Aetna and Evernorth require licensure where the member is located); parent-training requirements and treatment-plan goal format on all 21 Iowa, Missouri and New Mexico guides (no payer requires goals organized by DSM-5 criteria; NM Medicaid requires "ample units" of 97156/97157 with no PA on 97156). Also: Aetna Better Health NJ documentation rules (no named diagnostic instrument; licensed provider signs and countersigns technician entries); TRICARE West assessment-authorization steps; Georgia Medicaid decides every PA, assessment included, in 7 calendar days (+10 for supplemental documents); Indiana IEP-based ABA is billed by the school corporation fee-for-service with modifier TM, never to the MCO; Arizona ACOM 417 reissued effective 10/1/2026 with unchanged timelines. Whole-state gaps South Carolina and Connecticut logged for a state build.',
